AuraDE installation and recovery environment

Run `aurade-installer-start` to install AuraDE. It asks a few questions, shows
what it will do, and does not touch any disk until you confirm that disk by
name. It runs the graphical installer when this machine can display one and
the text installer when it cannot; both ask the same questions and run the
same engine.

Run `aurade-installer-tui` to go straight to the text installer. Add NO_COLOR=1
for a plain-text session, or AURADE_FORCE_TUI=1 to skip the graphics check.

Run `aurade-installer` for the older prompt-by-prompt flow.
Run `aurade-install --help` for noninteractive and image-based installs.
Run `aurade-recovery --help` for rollback and evidence collection.

WARNING: tty1 is a local installation console with an empty root password.
Do not expose this live session to an untrusted network or physical access.
Create a normal account password during installation; this live root account
is not copied to the installed system.
